Count all Digits of a Number

class Solution {
    public static int countDigits(int n) {
        // Code here
        int count=0;
        while(n > 0){
            int lastdigit=n%10;
            count++;
            n=n/10;
        }
        return count;
        
    }
}
Approach
Step 1: Observe the Pattern
Every time we divide a number by 10, the last digit gets removed.
I know that dividing a number by 10 removes its last digit. 
So I repeatedly divide the number by 10 until it becomes 0. 
Each division removes one digit, and I maintain a counter to track how many times this happens.
The final count gives the total number of digits in the number.

Most optimal Approach by using mathematical Log10
class Solution {
    public static int countDigits(int n) {
        // Code here
        int digits = (int) (Math.log10(n)) + 1;  
        return digits;
        
    }
}
The logic is based on logarithms. For a number n, if 10^k ≤n< 10k+1
, then it has k+1 digits. Taking base-10 logarithm gives k≤log10(n)<k+1. 
Therefore, floor(log10(n)) gives k, and adding 1 gives the total number of digits.
